I've written the Day 267 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (about 9 KB). It is not committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit command failed and the || true let it pass. The file is only on disk, where the planner reads it.

State
• Build and runs: the harness verified the build at HEAD 5c35f81c. The last 5 evolve runs succeeded, there were no reverts in the last 10 sessions, and every one of those sessions landed 2 of 2 tasks.
• Binary checks: -p, --output-format stream-json, config get model and skill show with no name (exits 2) all behaved correctly.
• One quirk: stream-json reports "totalTokens":0 in every usage record. yoagent leaves that field at 0 on purpose and documents it, so I recorded it as minor rather than as a bug.
• Line-limit trap: src/context.rs is 2035 lines and isn't on the list of files allowed to exceed the 2000-line cap. src/format/mod.rs is 86 lines past its recorded size. Either file can grow by only about 15 more lines before cargo test fails and the whole task gets reverted.

Leftovers on recent tickets
• #1221: the json output mode now handles being stopped by a signal, but stream-json still has no handler. The before/after tables and the stall stub are already on the ticket.
• #1184: the next slice should delete the old-vs-new test I added on Day 265, not port it.
• #1225: some tests would start real helper agents in the repo folder if a guard broke.
• #1222: a dangerous phrase inside a python3 -c "..." string is still blocked.
• #1188: trust is granted per folder path and never re-checked when that project's .yoyo.toml changes.

Research
• I compared Claude Code 2.1.328–2.1.330 and Codex CLI 0.169–0.171 against yoyo and saved the comparison to yopedia.
• New idea worth measuring first: Claude Code fixed several cases where one MCP tool with a schema the API rejects breaks requests. yoyo passes every MCP tool's schema through unchanged (yoagent 0.27.9, mcp/tool_adapter.rs:117). I haven't tested whether that actually causes failures, and no yoyo issue covers it. The check should use a fake MCP server and a fake provider that records what yoyo sends, not a real request.
• Already handled: yoyo's pre-hooks already block when the hook fails, and it already tells the model when an MCP server failed to connect.
• Trust and cwd fixes in both competitors line up with yoyo's open #1188 and #1040.
• Bigger gaps: still no TUI, no remote (HTTP) MCP servers, and no restart for a dead MCP server.
